WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.520
Meet the morning in a position that is safe and supported.

2
00:00:04.220 --> 00:00:07.060
You do not have to feel rested, positive, or ready.

3
00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:11.480
Begin with the morning that is actually here.

4
00:00:22.195 --> 00:00:23.395
Notice the light.

5
00:00:25.095 --> 00:00:29.625
It may be daylight, a lamp, or darkness that has not yet lifted.

6
00:00:31.325 --> 00:00:35.155
Let the eyes receive brightness and shadow without needing to judge the hour.

7
00:00:48.548 --> 00:00:50.398
Feel where the body is supported.

8
00:00:52.098 --> 00:00:55.128
Notice the weight of the feet, seat, back, or hands.

9
00:00:56.828 --> 00:01:03.908
If the body feels heavy, restless, or uncomfortable, that is information rather than a problem to solve in this moment.

10
00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:21.670
Let one natural breath move through.

11
00:01:23.370 --> 00:01:30.240
Notice where it is easiest to feel: nose, throat, chest, belly, or the movement of clothing.

12
00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:34.250
Leave the breath at its own depth and pace.

13
00:01:50.323 --> 00:01:53.873
The day may already be speaking in lists.

14
00:01:55.573 --> 00:01:58.693
Hear those plans without stepping into all of them.

15
00:02:00.393 --> 00:02:03.703
For now, let each item wait outside this single breath.

16
00:02:21.561 --> 00:02:23.071
Notice the inner weather.

17
00:02:24.771 --> 00:02:28.971
Clear or foggy, eager or reluctant, calm or busy.

18
00:02:30.671 --> 00:02:32.511
More than one quality can be present.

19
00:02:34.211 --> 00:02:36.141
No forecast is needed for the whole day.

20
00:02:52.213 --> 00:02:54.073
Choose one way you would like to meet the next hour.

21
00:02:55.773 --> 00:03:02.263
Perhaps steadily, kindly, directly, patiently, or with enough space to notice.

22
00:03:03.963 --> 00:03:07.203
Pick a word that feels workable rather than impressive.

23
00:03:25.061 --> 00:03:27.581
Feel how that word might appear in the body.

24
00:03:29.281 --> 00:03:35.691
It could mean easing the jaw, placing both feet down, looking at one thing at a time, or taking a pause before replying.

25
00:03:37.391 --> 00:03:39.691
Let the word become one small physical choice.

26
00:03:55.763 --> 00:03:58.983
Now name the first practical step after this meditation.

27
00:04:00.683 --> 00:04:07.213
Keep it close: drink water, open a curtain, wash, dress, eat, or begin one task.

28
00:04:08.913 --> 00:04:11.243
There is no need to organize the entire day here.

29
00:04:24.636 --> 00:04:25.696
Take in the room again.

30
00:04:27.396 --> 00:04:30.216
Notice light, sound, and support together.

31
00:04:31.916 --> 00:04:35.596
This morning does not need to resemble any other morning to count as a beginning.

32
00:04:48.990 --> 00:04:51.180
Move the hands and feet.

33
00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:55.080
Let the gaze settle toward your first step.

34
00:04:56.780 --> 00:05:00.000
Begin the day from where you are, at a pace you can inhabit.
